  "body": "## What changed\n`write_plate_stl()` in `crates/app/tests/box_pick.rs` wrote into a pid-named temp directory and removed it first. The two MCP tests of the binary share that path, so under parallel test threads one test deleted the other's `plate.stl` (`import_model` os error 3). Each call now gets its own directory (pid plus a process-wide atomic counter) and nothing is removed. Test code only.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test box_pick`, 3 runs, default threads: 7 passed each run.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test box_pick -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Pinning tests: `mcp_pick_in_box_adds_the_rim_in_one_undo_step`, `mcp_pick_in_box_is_visible_only_unless_through`.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe full batch and release tiers; the intermittent failure was not reproduced on purpose (it is a race), so the 3 clean runs are evidence, not proof.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1353\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
